{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"635c5531f951062a","name":"card_unit_31e_algiers","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/units/card_unit_31e_algiers","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"31e ALGÉRIENS","text":"Adjacent non-French units have +2 attack.","flavorText":"The 31st Regiment of Tirailleurs Algerians (31e RTA) was part of the 7th North African Infantry Division ( 7e DINA) of the French Army during WWII. The division was composed primarily of regiments from French North Africa, including Algeria, Tunisia, and Morocco, except for the 97th Reconnaissance Group which was a motorized cavalry unit composed of members of the French Foreign Legion. The division saw action while trying to defend positions near the Somme in 1940, but suffered such heavy losses that it was disbanded shortly after. It is worth mentioning that during WWII, approximately 290,000 Algerian soldiers fought with the Allies in the French Expeditionary Corps between 1943 and 1945, participating in the Italian campaign of 1943 and the invasion of southern France in 1944.","faction":"France","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_31e_algiers","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_31e_algiers_title","SourceString":"31e ALGÉRIENS","LocalizedString":"31e ALGÉRIENS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_31e_algiers_text","SourceString":"Adjacent non-French units have +2 attack.","LocalizedString":"Adjacent non-French units have +2 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_31e_algiers_history","SourceString":"The 31st Regiment of Tirailleurs Algerians (31e RTA) was part of the 7th North African Infantry Division ( 7e DINA) of the French Army during WWII. The division was composed primarily of regiments from French North Africa, including Algeria, Tunisia, and Morocco, except for the 97th Reconnaissance Group which was a motorized cavalry unit composed of members of the French Foreign Legion. The division saw action while trying to defend positions near the Somme in 1940, but suffered such heavy losses that it was disbanded shortly after. It is worth mentioning that during WWII, approximately 290,000 Algerian soldiers fought with the Allies in the French Expeditionary Corps between 1943 and 1945, participating in the Italian campaign of 1943 and the invasion of southern France in 1944.","LocalizedString":"The 31st Regiment of Tirailleurs Algerians (31e RTA) was part of the 7th North African Infantry Division ( 7e DINA) of the French Army during WWII. The division was composed primarily of regiments from French North Africa, including Algeria, Tunisia, and Morocco, except for the 97th Reconnaissance Group which was a motorized cavalry unit composed of members of the French Foreign Legion. The division saw action while trying to defend positions near the Somme in 1940, but suffered such heavy losses that it was disbanded shortly after. It is worth mentioning that during WWII, approximately 290,000 Algerian soldiers fought with the Allies in the French Expeditionary Corps between 1943 and 1945, participating in the Italian campaign of 1943 and the invasion of southern France in 1944."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isInPermanentPool":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLocationMoved","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardRevealed"],"hasBlitz":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/Spring2023Candidates/t_frenchies.t_frenchies","SubPathString":""},"artist":"French WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"Ass